pert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Arkansas remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential elections, and the baseline points to a roughly fifteen-point Republican margin. The 2026 midterms reinforced that picture: Sarah Huckabee Sanders won a second term as governor and Tom Cotton was re-elected to the Senate, with Republicans holding their dominance across the state.\n\nThere is no race-specific polling, no expert ratings, and no meaningful fundraising data for the presidential contest, so the forecast rests on state fundamentals. Democrats have shown some signs of life in the South, and Kentucky's governor campaigned in Arkansas arguing the party can compete, but that is aspirational rather than demonstrated. The race is rated Likely Republican with wide uncertainty, since a national wave could shift margins but would need to be unusually large to flip the state.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0496, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0891, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0924, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0872, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0872, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0887, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0862, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0722, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0785, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0905, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0932, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0789, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0869, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0907, "margin": -15.0},